  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Crazy Eights. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: 'Crazy Eights is a popular shedding card game, especially beloved by children. The objective is simple: be the first player to discard all your cards. Players take turns playing cards to a central discard pile, matching either the rank or suit of the top card. The eponymous "crazy" 8s are wild cards that can be played on anything and allow the player to change the suit.',
    objective: 'Shed cards efficiently and avoid being left in the losing position defined by the local round rule.',
    gameplay: 'Use a 36-card pack and play clockwise. Players take turns playing legal cards according to the family shedding rule, with the local variant determining when a player must pick up, pass, or continue. The game ends when the losing position is resolved.',
    keyRules: [
      'The standard source classifies Hahndreier as a shedding game.',
      'It uses a 36-card French-suited pack ranked ace high.',
      'Regional variants preserve different names and penalties but share the family shedding structure.',
